"<p>Configure notification channels under <strong>Settings → Notifications</strong> (<code>notification.manage</code> permission) to receive real-time alerts for jobs, backups, monitoring thresholds, TLS certificates, updates, and security events.</p>\n<h2>Supported Channels</h2>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n<table><thead><tr><th align=\"left\">Channel</th><th align=\"left\">Configuration</th><th align=\"left\">Notes</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td align=\"left\"><strong>Email (SMTP)</strong></td><td align=\"left\">Host, port (<code>587</code>/<code>465</code>), security (<code>STARTTLS</code>, <code>TLS</code>, or <code>None</code> on private network), credentials, from/to addresses.</td><td align=\"left\">Supports comma-separated recipient lists.</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\"><strong>Discord</strong></td><td align=\"left\">Discord channel Webhook URL.</td><td align=\"left\">Public HTTPS by default; optional private network toggle.</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\"><strong>Slack</strong></td><td align=\"left\">Slack Incoming Webhook URL.</td><td align=\"left\">Public HTTPS by default; optional private network toggle.</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\"><strong>Telegram</strong></td><td align=\"left\">Bot Token (from <code>@BotFather</code>) and numeric Chat ID or <code>@channelname</code>.</td><td align=\"left\">Bot must be a member of the target chat/channel.</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\"><strong>Webhook</strong></td><td align=\"left\">Endpoint URL + auto-generated 64-hex signing secret.</td><td align=\"left\">Sends a JSON <code>POST</code> signed with HMAC-SHA256 in the <code>x-nitrobase-signature</code> header (<code>x-nitrobase-timestamp</code>, <code>x-nitrobase-event</code>, <code>x-nitrobase-delivery</code>).</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<h2>Event Categories</h2>\n<p>Each channel lets you choose which events to subscribe to:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Jobs:</strong> Deployment/job failures &#x26; successes, Git build failures &#x26; deployments, scheduled task failures/skips, rejected push webhooks.</li>\n<li><strong>Backups:</strong> <code>backup.failed</code>, <code>backup.stale</code> (no successful backup within <code>BACKUP_STALE_DAYS</code>, default 2 days).</li>\n<li><strong>Monitoring:</strong> <code>alert.opened</code>, <code>alert.resolved</code>, <code>server.unreachable</code>, <code>server.reachable</code>.</li>\n<li><strong>Domains &#x26; certificates:</strong> <code>cert.expiring</code> (within 14 days), <code>cert.error</code>.</li>\n<li><strong>Updates:</strong> <code>app.update_available</code>, <code>app.update_rolled_back</code>, <code>app.update_failed</code>.</li>\n<li><strong>Security (Critical):</strong> <code>security.new_login</code> (sign-in from a new device/IP), <code>security.2fa_disabled</code>, and <code>security.secret_revealed</code> (opt-in).</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Reliability &#x26; Storm Protection</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Retries:</strong> Failed deliveries retry up to <code>4</code> attempts (<code>NOTIFY_MAX_ATTEMPTS</code>) with exponential backoff starting at <code>5s</code>.</li>\n<li><strong>Deduplication &#x26; Rate Limiting:</strong> Identical <code>(event, subject)</code> notifications on a channel are deduped for <code>30</code> minutes (<code>NOTIFY_DEDUPE_WINDOW_MS</code>), capped at <code>30</code> deliveries/hour per channel (<code>NOTIFY_RATE_LIMIT</code>).</li>\n<li><strong>Critical bypass:</strong> Security events (<code>security.new_login</code>, <code>security.2fa_disabled</code>, <code>security.secret_revealed</code>) are <strong>never</strong> deduped or rate-limited so an alert storm can never hide a security incident.</li>\n<li><strong>Localization:</strong> Notification messages use <code>NOTIFY_LOCALE</code> (default <code>en</code>, supports <code>vi</code>). Delivery history is retained for <code>30</code> days.</li>\n</ul>"